<!--
  The mark's two shapes: a copper coin at rest in a shallow open cradle.

  Construction rules from DESIGN.md section 7, which is binding:
    - The coin rests at the cradle's lowest point, touching it. Never sunk into
      it, never floating above it.
    - The cradle is a stroke, the coin is a fill. That pairing is what keeps the
      mark two shapes.
    - The arc is shallow, its ends level with each other, stopping short of the
      frame so the arc breathes.
    - Nothing else is in frame. Flat: no gradients, no glow, no dimension.

  Drawn inside the 72x72 safe zone of the 108x108 adaptive icon canvas, so no
  launcher mask can clip the coin or the cradle's ends.
-->
<vector xmlns:android="http://schemas.android.com/apk/res/android"
    android:width="108dp"
    android:height="108dp"
    android:viewportWidth="108"
    android:viewportHeight="108">

    <!-- The cradle. Two quadratics form the shallow lower arc; its ends finish
         level with each other at y=55.3. -->
    <path
        android:pathData="M32.2,55.3 Q32.2,72.5 54,72.5 Q75.8,72.5 75.8,55.3"
        android:strokeColor="#AE6738"
        android:strokeWidth="1.78"
        android:strokeLineCap="round" />

    <!-- The coin. Its lower edge touches the inside of the cradle stroke at the
         cradle's lowest point: center 63.0, radius 8.58, so the coin's bottom
         reaches 71.58 and the stroke's inner edge sits at 72.5 - 0.89 = 71.61.
         Those two meeting is the construction rule, not a coincidence. The
         remaining 0.03 is a seventh of a pixel at the 512 store size, below
         anything that can be drawn; tools/make-store-art.py asserts it stays
         there. The fractions they come from live in ui/components/Mark.kt. -->
    <path
        android:pathData="M54,63.0 m-8.58,0 a8.58,8.58 0 1,0 17.16,0 a8.58,8.58 0 1,0 -17.16,0"
        android:fillColor="#AE6738" />
</vector>
